<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I work on generative AI at Amazon, building agent tooling and the backend
    services behind it. Before that I studied computer science at Georgia Tech
    and spent three summers at Qualcomm, on 5G modem software and an ML model
    that caught RF signal errors.
  </p>
  <p>
    The problem I keep coming back to is agents that keep working when nobody's
    watching. Most of my side projects are some piece of that: agents with
    memory that run for weeks, the tools they call, and the self-hosted
    infrastructure underneath.
  </p>
  <p>
    The code is on <a href="https://github.com/harshanchenna">GitHub</a>, and I'm on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/harshanchenna">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
